.TH GIT-WT 1 "July 27, 2026" "git-wt" "Git Manual"
.SH NAME
git-wt \- manage and open project-oriented Git worktrees
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git wt
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ arguments ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git wt
is an optional manual convenience for project-oriented Git worktrees.
With no command, it runs
.BR "git wt list" .
Writable lanes live beneath
.IR ~/worktrees/<owner>/<repository>/<lane> .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.I <branch>
Open or create a worktree for a branch.
.TP
.BI "issue " number " [--no-link-env]"
Create or reuse durable issue lane
.BR GH-<number> .
.TP
.BI "add " branch " [--no-link-env]"
Open an existing local or origin branch.
.TP
.BI "pr " number
Create or refresh detached inspection lane
.BR PR-<number> .
.TP
.BI "repair " number " [--no-link-env]"
Open a same-repository pull request's writable head branch.
.TP
.B list
List this clone's worktrees without pruning. This is the default command.
.TP
.B sync [--dry-run] [--json]
Reconcile origin and proven merged worktree lanes.
.TP
.B home
Open a shell in this clone's primary worktree.
.TP
.B root
Print the canonical linked-worktree directory.
.TP
.BI "path " lane
Print an exact registered lane path for shell navigation.
.TP
.BI "cd " lane
Open an interactive shell in an exact registered lane.
.TP
.BI "remove " lane-or-path
Remove one exact clean, fully-pushed worktree.
.TP
.B prune [--dry-run]
Explicitly prune stale worktree metadata.
.TP
.B migrate [--apply]
Preview or apply legacy flat-directory migration.
.TP
.B help
Show command help.
.SH LIST OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--sort " attribute
Sort by
.BR updated ,
.BR state ,
.BR head ,
or
.BR path .
.TP
.BI "--root-position " position
Pin the primary worktree at
.B top
(the default) or
.BR bottom .
.TP
.B --reverse
Reverse the selected sort order.
.TP
.B --plain
Print the table instead of opening the terminal selector.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GIT_WT_ROOT
Override
.IR ~/worktrees ,
primarily for testing.
.SH SAFETY
Detached
.B PR-<number>
lanes are inspection-only; use
.B repair
for edits. Writable lanes link the primary checkout's
.B .env
by default; use
.B --no-link-env
for isolation.
.B .envrc
is never linked automatically.
.PP
The
.B remove
command never forces, deletes a branch, or discards dirty or unpushed state.
No command stashes, resets, cleans, or force-removes worktrees.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git-worktree (1)
